{
 "case": "N18-EXCHANGE-NEG",
 "says": "Alice founds a Team and configures a Slack connection whose code exchange needs a client secret; the connection declares that the exchange runs in a Team-protected process she operates, and the stored connection carries no secret. A connection submitted with its client secret, and one declaring a protected exchange without saying who operates it, are refused at admission. She begins linking her Slack identity: a callback carrying the identity token itself is refused at admission, and the callback carrying only the verified claims links her identity, returning sign-in evidence and a binding with no token or secret in either. A Team permit carrying a refresh token is refused at admission when her device tries to keep it. What must not happen: a secret or token stored in the connection, the evidence, the binding or any record kept on the client.",
